### Goal Model Decomposition

#### Goal Nodes

| Name       | GOAL_ID: GOAL_TEXT | GOAL_RUNTIME_ANNOT | Goal Type       | Relation | Justification |
|------------|--------------------|--------------------|-----------------|----------|---------------|
| Mission    | G1: Manage Mission | ;                  | Achieve        | -        | Top-level goal for the entire mission. |
| Collection | G2: Collect Resources | ;                  | Perform        | AND      | Sequential execution of collection tasks. |
| Delivery   | G3: Deliver Resources | ;                  | Perform        | AND      | Sequential execution of delivery tasks. |

#### Sub-Goal Nodes

| Name                     | GOAL_ID: GOAL_TEXT                          | GOAL_RUNTIME_ANNOT | Goal Type       | Target Condition/Enquired Information | Relation | Justification |
|--------------------------|---------------------------------------------|--------------------|-----------------|-----------------------------------------|----------|---------------|
| Select Order             | G2.1: Select Collection Order               |                    | Perform         | Order based on waiting time and path   | AND      | Sequential step in collection. |
| Request Resources        | G2.2: Request Resources from Storage         |                    | Perform         | Resources retrieved from storage       | AND      | Sequential step in collection. |
| Handle Low Battery       | G2.3: Handle Low Battery in Collection       |                    | Achieve         | Mission continues with another robot   | AND      | Ensures mission continuity. |
| Deliver Resources        | G3.1: Deliver Resources to Destination       |                    | Perform         | Resources delivered to destination     | AND      | Sequential step in delivery. |
| Return to Checkpoint     | G3.2: Return Resources to Checkpoint        |                    | Achieve         | Resources at checkpoint, mission continues | AND      | Ensures resources are secured. |
| Ensure Delivery          | G3.3: Ensure All Resources Delivered        |                    | Achieve         | All resources delivered to destination  | AND      | Final delivery confirmation. |

#### Task Nodes

| Name                     | TASK_ID: TASK_NAME | Text                          | Relation | Location               | Number of Robots | Justification |
|--------------------------|-------------------|-------------------------------|----------|------------------------|------------------|---------------|
| Select Order             | AT1: SelectOrder   | Select optimal collection path | AND      | Storage locations     | 1                | Single robot for optimal path selection. |
| Request Resources        | AT2: RequestRes    | Request resources from storage | AND      | Storage locations     | 1                | Single robot per storage request. |
| Handle Low Battery       | AT3: Recharge     | Recharge and assign mission    | AND      | Recharging station    | 1                | Ensures mission continuity. |
| Deliver Resources        | AT4: DeliverRes    | Deliver resources to location  | AND      | Destination location  | 1                | Single robot for delivery. |
| Return to Checkpoint     | AT5: ReturnRes    | Return resources to checkpoint | AND      | Checkpoint location   | 1                | Ensures resource security. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**
  - Justification: Both collection and delivery are essential for mission success, hence sequential execution.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2, G2.3 [AND]**
  - Justification: Each step in collection must be completed in sequence.

- **G2.1 -> AT1 [AND]**
  - Justification: Selecting the order is a necessary step before requesting resources.

- **G2.2 -> AT2 [AND]**
  - Justification: Directly executes the request action.

- **G2.3 -> AT3 [AND]**
  - Justification: Ensures mission continuity upon low battery.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2, G3.3 [AND]**
  - Justification: Each step in delivery must be completed in sequence.

- **G3.1 -> AT4 [AND]**
  - Justification: Executes the delivery action.

- **G3.2 -> AT5 [AND]**
  - Justification: Ensures resources are secure if delivery is interrupted.

- **G3.3 -> - [AND]**
  - Justification: Confirmation of delivery completion.

This structured approach ensures that each part of the mission is handled efficiently, with clear execution paths and contingency plans for potential issues.
